Installing ArgoCD on Kubernetes

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m doing a hands-on setup of Argo CD on Kubernetes. 🚀
This is a crucial step to start working with real GitOps workflows in a live environment.

🔹 Prerequisites
Before installing ArgoCD, make sure you have:
A running Kubernetes cluster
kubectl installed and configured
Basic understanding of Kubernetes resources

🔹 Installation Steps

1️⃣ Create Namespace:-
kubectl create namespace argocd
 
2️⃣ Install ArgoCD:-
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://lnkd.in/dPY5uSn9

3️⃣ Check Pods Status:-
kubectl get pods -n argocd

4️⃣ Access ArgoCD API Server:-
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443

Now open in browser:
👉 https://localhost:8080

5️⃣ Get Initial Admin Password:-
kubectl get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -n argocd -o yaml

Decode the password and login using:
Username: admin
Password: (decoded value)

💡 Key Insight:
Installing ArgoCD on Kubernetes allows you to automate deployments directly from Git repositories, enabling a complete GitOps workflow.
